requirements.detail:
To account for deflection, bending, and warping during hot metal forming, the standard increases both machining allowances and dimensional tolerances for slender forgings based on the ratio of length (b) to section size (a):
a) For b/a <= 7: Normal working allowances and tolerances apply as per Tables 1, 2, and 3;
b) For b/a <= 8: Increase size-specific allowances and tolerances by 15 percent;
c) For b/a <= 9: Increase size-specific allowances and tolerances by 30 percent;
d) For b/a <= 10: Increase size-specific allowances and tolerances by 75 percent;
e) For b/a > 10: Specific allowances and tolerances must be mutually agreed between the manufacturer and the purchaser on an individual basis.
